1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:04,368
(Q1) Good morning. World Tours. My name is Jamie. How can I help you?

2
00:00:04,368 --> 00:00:10,035
Good morning. I want some information on self-drive tours in the USA.

3
00:00:10,035 --> 00:00:11,536
Could you send me a brochure?

4
00:00:11,536 --> 00:00:13,864
Of course. Could I have your name please?

5
00:00:13,864 --> 00:00:15,768
(QExample) Andrea Brown.&nbsp;

6
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:18,031
Thank you. And your address?

7
00:00:18,031 --> 00:00:20,480
24. Ardleigh Road.&nbsp;

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,815
Can you spell that?

9
00:00:21,815 --> 00:00:27,122
[Q1答案句] A-R-D-L-E-I-G-H Road.&nbsp;

10
00:00:27,122 --> 00:00:28,489
(Q2) Postcode?

11
00:00:28,489 --> 00:00:32,088
BH520P&nbsp;

12
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:34,655
Thanks. And can I have your phone number?

13
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:36,344
Is a mobile alright?

14
00:00:36,344 --> 00:00:37,056
Fine.

15
00:00:37,056 --> 00:00:44,240
It's 07786643091.

16
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:50,633
Thank you. And can I ask you where you heard about World Tours? From a friend? Or did you see an advert somewhere?

17
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:53,131
[Q2答案句] No, I read about you in the newspaper.

18
00:00:53,131 --> 00:00:58,283
OK, I'll get the brochures in the post to you but can I give you some information over the phone.

19
00:00:58,283 --> 00:01:01,569
(Q3) What kinds of things do you want to do on your holiday?

20
00:01:01,569 --> 00:01:08,607
I'm interested in going to California with my family. I've got two children and we want to hire a car.

21
00:01:08,607 --> 00:01:14,897
OK. We have a couple of self-drive tours there visiting different places of interest in California.

22
00:01:14,897 --> 00:01:20,325
[Q3答案句] The first one begins in Los Angeles and there's plenty of time to visit some of the theme parks there.

23
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:24,433
That's something on my children's list so I'd want to include that.

24
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:27,688
(Q4) Good. Then you drive to San Francisco.

25
00:01:27,688 --> 00:01:32,890
From San Francisco you can drive to Yosemite Park where you spend a couple of nights.

26
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:36,611
You can choose to stay in a lodge or on the campsite.

27
00:01:36,611 --> 00:01:40,650
[Q4答案句] I don't like the idea of staying in a tent. It'd be too hot.

28
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:43,759
Right. And the tour ends in Las Vegas.

29
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:44,692
OK.

30
00:01:44,692 --> 00:01:52,012
(Q5) The other trip we can arrange is slightly different. It starts in San Francisco. Then you drive south to Cambria.

31
00:01:52,012 --> 00:01:57,317
[Q5答案句] Someone told me there's a really nice castle near Cambria. Will we go near that?

32
00:01:57,317 --> 00:02:00,691
Hearst Castle is on that road so you could stop there.

33
00:02:00,691 --> 00:02:02,907
Good. I'd like to do that.&nbsp;

34
00:02:02,907 --> 00:02:05,558
(Q6) Does this trip also go into the desert?

35
00:02:05,558 --> 00:02:10,396
No, it continues to Santa Monica where most people like to stop and do some shopping.

36
00:02:10,396 --> 00:02:14,335
We have enough of that at home so that doesn't interest us.

37
00:02:14,335 --> 00:02:17,958
OK. Well you could go straight on to San Diego.

38
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:20,412
[Q6答案句] That's good for beaches isn't it?

39
00:02:20,412 --> 00:02:26,351
That's right, that's a good place to relax and your children might like to visit the zoo before flying home.

40
00:02:26,351 --> 00:02:32,528
I don't think so. We want some time for sunbathing and swimming.

41
00:02:32,528 --> 00:02:37,211
(Q7（table横纵表格填空）) So how many days are the trips and how much do they cost?

42
00:02:37,211 --> 00:02:46,544
The first one I told you about is a self-drive tour through California which lasts twelve days and covers 2,020 kilometres.

43
00:02:46,544 --> 00:02:57,465
The shortest journey is 206 km and the longest is 632 kilometres. The cost is £525 per person.

44
00:02:57,465 --> 00:03:02,033
That includes accommodation, car rental and a flight but no meals.

45
00:03:02,033 --> 00:03:04,533
OK. And the other trip?

46
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:11,855
That lasts nine days but you spend only three days on the road. You cover about 980 kilometres altogether.

47
00:03:11,855 --> 00:03:13,658
So is that cheaper then?

48
00:03:13,658 --> 00:03:19,573
Yes, it's almost a hundred pounds cheaper. It's £429 per person, which is a good deal.

49
00:03:19,573 --> 00:03:24,726
So that covers accommodation and car hire. What about flights?

50
00:03:24,726 --> 00:03:28,610
They aren't included. But these hotels offer dinner in the price.

51
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:34,622
OK. Well, thank you very much. I'll be in touch when I've had a chance to look at the brochure.

52
00:03:34,622 --> 00:03:36,311
I'm pleased to help. Goodbye.

53
00:03:36,311 --> 00:03:38,811
Goodbye.

